    "vulnerabilities_and_strategic_counter_arguments": {
      "dismantling_renckton_leblanc_corki_defense": "Paragraph 1 explicitly sets the baseline definition of Dash-Flash: using Flash during the dash to 'make use of the buffer and land the dash more efficient.' Renekton E, Corki W, LeBlanc W, and Nidalee W fail this threshold at step one (they cannot buffer Flash during the dash without canceling it or locking out). An author does not write a specific operational caveat in Paragraph 2 to filter out abilities that already fail the basic definition in Paragraph 1. Furthermore, off-list champions (Lucian, Graves, Vayne) cannot serve as the answer key for a multiple-choice question of 26 listed champions.",
      "active_buffered_delivery_vs_passive_model_displacement": "Tryndamere's E has zero input buffering in the engine. It is an uninterruptible moving aura. Flashing mid-spin merely displaces his coordinates; the damage tick upon arrival is incidental to closing distance for follow-up basic attacks. It does not 'buffer the dash to land it more efficiently.'",
